Task 1: Define Routes Using Java DSL
Subtask 1.1: Create a Basic File Route
Create a Java Class (FileRoute.java):
package com.example;

import org.apache.camel.builder.RouteBuilder;

public class FileRoute extends RouteBuilder {
    @Override
    public void configure() throws Exception {
        from("file:data/input?noop=true")
            .log("File received: ${file:name}")
            .to("file:data/output");
    }
}
Run the Route
package com.example;

import org.apache.camel.main.Main;

public class App {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        Main main = new Main();
        main.configure().addRoutesBuilder(new FileRoute());
        main.run();
    }
}
Expected Outcome
Place a file in data/input.
The file will be moved to data/output with a log message.
Subtask 1.2: HTTP to File Route
Modify FileRoute.java
from("jetty:http://localhost:8080/myEndpoint")
    .log("HTTP Request received: ${body}")
    .to("file:data/http-output");
Test with curl
curl -X POST -d "Hello Camel" http://localhost:8080/myEndpoint
Expected Outcome
The HTTP request body is saved in data/http-output.
Task 2: Define Routes Using XML DSL
Subtask 2.1: Create camel-context.xml
Add XML Configuration (src/main/resources/META-INF/spring/camel-context.xml):
<camelContext xmlns="http://camel.apache.org/schema/spring">
    <route>
        <from uri="file:data/xml-input?noop=true"/>
        <log message="XML File processed: ${file:name}"/>
        <to uri="file:data/xml-output"/>
    </route>
</camelContext>
Run with Spring
import org.springframework.context.support.ClassPathXmlApplicationContext;

public class App {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        new ClassPathXmlApplicationContext("META-INF/spring/camel-context.xml");
        Thread.sleep(5000); // Keep the app running
    }
}
Expected Outcome
Files in data/xml-input are moved to data/xml-output.
Task 3: Test Route Functionality
Subtask 3.1: JMS Integration (ActiveMQ)
Add ActiveMQ Dependency (pom.xml):
<dependency>
    <groupId>org.apache.activemq</groupId>
    <artifactId>activemq-camel</artifactId>
    <version>5.16.6</version>
</dependency>
Create a JMS Route (JmsRoute.java):
from("activemq:queue:testQueue")
    .log("JMS Message: ${body}")
    .to("file:data/jms-output");
Send a Test Message
camel-jms producer --destination testQueue --message "Hello JMS"
Expected Outcome
The message is logged and saved in data/jms-output.
